      "writtenOn": "2022-08-19T13:37:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "@Isaac: We are calling, the swusp_check, via a hibernation script in userspace, triggered, after boot to HMI and post module loading.\nuserspace echo (major:minor number of the swap block device)\n\u003d\u003eresume_store\n  \u003d\u003esoftware_resume\n   \u003d\u003eswsusp_check\n   \u003d\u003etrace_android_vh_check_randomization(p-\u003ebdev, \u0026noswap_randomize)\n     \nRegarding the usage of GENHD_FL_NO_RANDOMIZE  within gendisk flags, yes, for now we are using this, as we have to mark the swap device in some manner, I could have used a Android vendor field, but that would have modified a core data structure, let me know if you have better ideas.",
      "parentUuid": "5a1fc93e_55b1b77c",
      "revId": "f0175ec5e6ec04be647f3dc298b759f6ec3e6b3e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
